// src/v4/std/diagnostic.dag
//
// Scope: fail-closed Diagnostic schema with structural reason+at+correction.
//        Per STRUCTURE.md architectural commitment #3, the schema CARRIES
//        the suggested-correction obligation — the substrate must be able
//        to enforce THESIS:103-105 "show the correct code", so the field
//        is part of the type, not optional bolt-on.
// Anchor: THESIS.md "Show the correct code" §103-105 + INVARIANTS P3
//
// Owns:
//   - Diagnostic { reason: NamedReason, at: Locus, correction: Correction }
//   - NamedReason enum (structural; never opaque string)
//   - Locus = port|node|file|span
//   - Correction = Suggested(Node) | Unavailable(NoCorrectionReason)
//     (typed sum — NOT Option<Node>. "no correction available" is
//     a structural Unavailable case carrying a NoCorrectionReason, never a
//     bare None enforced by convention. Type-enforced per INVARIANTS P2,
//     not API-enforced.)
//     The suggested correction is a Node — the bounded kernel says Node is
//     the ONLY recursive type, so a subtree of Nodes IS a Node (no separate
//     "NodeFragment": that would be a decorative alias the compiler sees
//     through, per feedback_nodes_are_nodes + feedback_naming_is_aliasing).
//     WHERE the correction applies is not carried by the fragment — it is
//     the Diagnostic's own `at: Locus`.
//   - NoCorrectionReason = closed enum (UserInputBoundary | AmbiguousIntent
//     | ExternalContractUnknown | ...) — every "no fix" answers WHY structurally
//
// Consumes:
//   - std/node.dag: Conj, Disj
//   - std/primitive.dag: String for messages
//
// Status: scaffold — fill per TASKS.md T-3
// Brief: see BRIEF_TEMPLATE.md; this file's I/O contract is the immutable
// contract for the worker. Splitting this file requires explicit operator
// ratification (substrate extension = stop signal).


module v4.std.diagnostic

